 once in the shared projection primitive; distinguish absent, empty, omitted, and inapplicable groups in typed receipts; ensure explicit budgets still bind; add unit, integration, packed-consumer, and executable recovery negative controls; document the compatibility contract and token-cost impact."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make every explicit read projection self-identifying and preserve requested empty collections as meaningful data."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents can distinguish an empty requested group from an omitted group without paying for unrelated item context."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Successful projected reads can carry neither identity nor requested data, so automation cannot associate, interpret, or safely recover the result."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"The shared SDK read projection contract retains minimum identity and explicitly requested empty values across CLI, SDK, MCP, and all item read aliases."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"GitHub #1033 demonstrates a new silent-data-loss class at the universal projection boundary."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Current pm read/get fields projection on 2026-08-15"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Read an item whose selected linked collection is empty using pm read <id> --fields <group>; inspect the result for the item id, the requested empty collection, and omission semantics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"The result includes stable item identity and the explicitly selected empty collection while omitting only unrequested groups with executable recovery receipts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The result can omit id and the requested field and return only groups the caller excluded, despite a zero exit status."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-cxr0jb","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-15T15:27:12.262Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-15T15:27:12.262Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for GH-1033, fields empty group, requested empty collection, identity projection, and omission receipt found no item for this exact zero-exit projection failure. Closed pm-cxr0jb and pm-p258tx provide intent-projection and omission-receipt lineage; open pm-5t33or is the canonical universal output parent. This issue records the newly reported regression without duplicating those items."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"06008be4a62504abc1a56a06802f7ba2174ca4536bae82b46525cf5b3139246f","item_hash_version":2,"message":""}
